{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted","id":1277743,"title":"So Lookshy has what like a hundred times the Concentration of Exalted?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-31T18:39:43-08:00","id":1277743,"title":"So Lookshy has what like a hundred times the Concentration of Exalted?","content":"So I\u2019m seeing that Prasad has a good number of Dragonblooded, 2k. That\u2019s very respectable since the Terrestrials of the Dragonblooded had a lot of planning and clout to achieve and Prasad has 2k, could it be because two failed houses evacuated to the empire bolstering probably an already respectable number of DB. But Lookshy is a city state with 3k DB!<br /> <br /> Did you think they were just prudent and didn\u2019t want to insert a new culture and have them have more Dragonblooded then Lookshy since that is Lookshy\u2019s thing?<br /> <br /> So if you have a small cities worth of Dragonblooded living in a city they are going to have insanely concentrated blood?<br /> <br /> Or do you think Lookshy keeps smaller settlements all over the river province? It kind of feels they should be more then just a city state? Or do they have a diaspora where Lookshy citizens exist in many nations but still have loyalties towards Lookshy?<br /> <br /> I mean how many Manses can one City state have? For normal places it would be one Manse, but probably should control like over a dozen just for their Artifacts and what not alone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-31T22:20:58-08:00","id":1277771,"title":"","content":"As I recall, and I admit my memory on this is faded, lookshy has a kind of series of satellite settlements and redoubts that serve to project its power and influence over a much larger area than you would expect. It may also have a network of vassal states and such the like that make their number still insanely concentrated, but somewhat more dilute.<br /> <br /> Apologies for any lack of clairity in this post, I have been making rather merry this New Year\u2019s Eve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-31T23:29:24-08:00","id":1277776,"title":"","content":"Okay yeah in can see them with protectorates or extended across the river province as a defense force.<br /> <br /> Have a happy Calibration you Twin Fisted Merry Maker you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T00:10:17-08:00","id":1277782,"title":"","content":"Firstly Lookshy has an aggressive adoption policy toward all Lost Eggs in the River Province/Scavenger Lands. And unlike with the Realm and Prasad, the Lost Eggs are full equal members with other DBs in their society as members of the Gents that adopt them. This is a huge factor in their numbers. And yeah, as I treat it, each \u201credoubt\u201d is a full city state scale satellite of Lookshy society, in addition to almost every adult DB actively serving in the Legion wherever it\u2019s various For E\u2019s are stationed, so their DBs are not hyper-concentrated in the city proper.<br /> <br /> Though Lookshy likely does have the highest Exalted PER CAPITA numbers in Creation. The Imperial City has higher DBs total, but lower than Lookshy-proper per capita as it\u2019s also a massive mortal trade center. No comment on where the capital of Prasad fits on that spectrum until I read more about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T00:31:02-08:00","id":1277783,"title":"","content":"Wait really the Imperial City you think had more then City of Lookshy residing within?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T00:42:47-08:00","id":1277786,"title":"","content":"More specifically, the Dynasty is concerned with keeping powerful, pure bloodlines, Lookshy focuses more on quantity over quality. It's little surprise they'd have a lot of Exalted, but none of them will have high breeding (and many might have the flaw for <i>weak</i> breeding).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T01:08:44-08:00","id":1277789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted#post1277743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I\u2019m seeing that Prasad has a good number of Dragonblooded, 2k. That\u2019s very respectable since the Terrestrials of the Dragonblooded had a lot of planning and clout to achieve and Prasad has 2k, could it be because two failed houses evacuated to the empire bolstering probably an already respectable number of DB.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Prasad's Houses were failing. I think they saw an opportunity in how much power they could world so far from home, and sneakily relocated entirely.<br /> <br /> A thousand per House is about right for the Realm as well, give or take (looking at Nellens and V'neef).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you think they were just prudent and didn\u2019t want to insert a new culture and have them have more Dragonblooded then Lookshy since that is Lookshy\u2019s thing?<br /> <br /> So if you have a small cities worth of Dragonblooded living in a city they are going to have insanely concentrated blood?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lookshy basically pulls double duty as both itself, and most of the River Province when it comes to Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or do you think Lookshy keeps smaller settlements all over the river province? It kind of feels they should be more then just a city state? Or do they have a diaspora where Lookshy citizens exist in many nations but still have loyalties towards Lookshy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lookshy is kind of hemmed in within its own fortified city, by it's archnemesis to the west and its own allies east.<br /> <br /> Lookshy's power is well concentrated, but still less than the Realm's. It spreads its strength too far and thin, the city becomes a more tempting target to the Dynasty.<br /> <br /> Lookshy's choice in having people to effectively expand over are fellow River Province states, and the Realm invasions showed how troublesome they are to control. Where else are you going to try colonising? So far from home that the communication lines are stretched and vulnerable? Encroaching on satrapies, and provoking further war with the Realm?<br /> <br /> And Lookshy is also at risk from Lunars. I propose that in their current state, they're harassed a lot less than the Realm, but if they acted in a manner provacative and exposing...<br /> <br /> Of course, these are the arguments of the policy faction that controls the city. It's always been written to have people who <i>advocate</i> for imperialism. One can make stories out of their day coming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean how many Manses can one City state have? For normal places it would be one Manse, but probably should control like over a dozen just for their Artifacts and what not alone!</div> </div> </div> </div>What do they need manses for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T01:25:30-08:00","id":1277793,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a>: You seem to forget that many Hearthstones as of Ex3 are generated by demesnes, or even just crystallize out of the Wyld. Also, the number of artifacts that require Hearthstones to get functionality out of is significantly lower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T01:56:11-08:00","id":1277795,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m using manse as shorthand for demesnes and Hearthstones in general. And I said dozens instead of hundreds because I took into account the changes.<br /> <br /> Anyone else to weigh in? One person says one Citystate is enough for an Empires worth of Dragonblooded and others are saying most of Lookshys Dragonblooded aren\u2019t in Lookshy, and another feels the fortresses and military stations are essentially towns and they build around the Scavenger Lands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T02:14:33-08:00","id":1277796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1277795#post1277795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One person says one Citystate is enough for an Empires worth of Dragonblooded</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a simplification. For one thing, I expect most of Prasad's Exalted live in its capital, because it's nicer. They don't need to equally distribute them across the empire to maintain authority.<br /> <br /> For another, I was not arguing that it's &quot;enough&quot;, I'm saying that they're kind of stuck within their current boundaries, and many within find that uncomfortable and argue for spreading out.<br /> <br /> That being said, Lookshy's business probably ensures that many are far away at any given time, just not for administering territory or personal pursuits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T02:32:10-08:00","id":1277798,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think most of Prasad\u2019s Dragon Caste will be in Kamthahar because I imagine like the realm households will have Estates all over the Empire built upon Manses. Easier to play God when there are less Gods per square Mile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T04:27:42-08:00","id":1277809,"title":"","content":"Exalted deal with buildings other than manses, y'know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T11:35:27-08:00","id":1277875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1277809#post1277809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted deal with buildings other than manses, y'know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I know, we also have Demesnes! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Why fade when you can star wipe?<br /> <br /> Seriously this is how Dragonblooded have been portrayed handling their bases of operations, they are even called Manses for gods sake.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s like asking \u201chuh I wonder why they keep building cities near major trade routes, rivers and coasts.\u201d<br /> <br /> Mortals build houses or temples anywhere, Powerful Exalts, and living Gods like the Dragon Caste who rule Prasad build on Manses, why wouldn\u2019t they the benefits are tangible and obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T13:20:10-08:00","id":1277909,"title":"","content":"I'm not even going to touch that, for the sake of preserving the topic.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Lookshy. Another thing that I think helps them is not cultivating so much entitlement in the Exalted (especially since a majority of their Exalted may not be in the major families). They're less aristocratic, so there's less necessary real estate per Exalt. Really, less expenses all round; in the Realm, the nature of their society and how they manage their Exalted makes it more costly to be one, so you've got systems such as the government takes on some of the burden, and the revenue streams that need to be made available to them. Hell, their distribution across the Isle might be a thing partially engineered by the Empress, for reasons such as diffusing their power, and in combination with the social scene of their galas to be another thing that occupies their attention and consumes their resources.<br /> <br /> Lookshy's needs and priorities are different, less competitive, less anxious, less materialist. They can keep more of their Exalted closer together, and devote their energy to different purposes.<br /> <br /> The sense I get from Prasad, mostly from what I can vaguely recall of the satrapy write-up preview, gives me the image of a society that largely only interacts with itself, tightly knit and living in the physical upper strata of the major city; Yu-Shan in miniature on Earth. <br /> <br /> Certainly, the idea of one's godliness being tied to scarcity seems a bit out of place in a setting where gods number in the millions. I expect the Exalted of Prasad to be more akin to the court of Golden-Eyed Jorst than a system in which every county needs its one true god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T13:29:13-08:00","id":1277911,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s my point some Major Gods leave Yu-Shan to make court on Creation where they are a bigger deal.<br /> <br /> And Prasad interacts with themselves, they are expanding against smaller neighbors and making war and trade with rival empires, and the pledge to the realm because that helps with Trade across the rest of Creation. So they aren\u2019t really isolated and only talking with themselves the ar expansionist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T20:09:02-08:00","id":1277983,"title":"","content":"Also, I think it's worth remembering that a city-state != a city. Though they take their names from the main urban center (usually a political, economic, and military hub) a city-state can represent significant territory. For example, Attica (the area controlled by the classical Athens city-state) was/is nearly 1000 square miles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T09:40:46-08:00","id":1278091,"title":"","content":"There could also be a decent amount of DBs dispersed throughout the Confederation of Rivers. A coalition of so many disparate cultures is both ripe with opportunities for learning and growth, as well as a heavy reliance on trade and diplomacy. Combine that with the fact that Lookshy is one of the biggest protectors of the river province as a whole and you\u2019ve got military DBs off on mercenary contracts and peacekeeping/deterrent missions, traders and merchants travelling all over hammering out new deals, diplomats stationed all over the place, all kinds of things. They all identify very strongly as Lookshy nationals but they might live hundreds of miles from the city and not have been there in years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T23:36:22-08:00","id":1278256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1277783#post1277783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait really the Imperial City you think had more then City of Lookshy residing within?</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually. Most of Lookshy\u2019s DBs are on active deployment at any given time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T01:31:57-08:00","id":1278266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1277983#post1277983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I think it's worth remembering that a city-state != a city. Though they take their names from the main urban center (usually a political, economic, and military hub) a city-state can represent significant territory. For example, Attica (the area controlled by the classical Athens city-state) was/is nearly 1000 square miles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that depends on what one count as significant, as that is the size of a square with the side of 32 miles, or a circle with a radius of 18 miles. Pretty much everything is at least within one day of forced marching from the city. So pretty much one city, a handful of towns, and a bunch of villages.<br /> <br /> So city-state = a city + the support system to keep it fed and able to defend itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","user":"Lundgren","date":". 01-03-2019, 04:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T05:23:59-08:00","id":1278289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1277783#post1277783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait really the Imperial City you think had more then City of Lookshy residing within?</div> </div> </div> </div>The nature of the Realm's power structure makes it very plausible that the majority of Dynastic Dragon-Blooded live in or near the Imperial City and regard even a prestigious assignment elsewhere as a form of exile. I wouldn't ever advocate for it but it makes sense from a top-down view of the Realm as an empire that the 10,000 people with the most influence would live in the capital.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T05:35:27-08:00","id":1278290,"title":"","content":"Don't each of the Great Houses have a main territory somewhere on the Blessed Isle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T05:41:28-08:00","id":1278291,"title":"","content":"The Second Edition Blessed Isle book said something to the effect that about half of the Scarlet Dynasty reside in the Imperial City, primarily the palace (which is really more of a miniature city within it) at any given time.<br /> <br /> One might also draw upon many historical systems in which a period of residence at the royal or imperial court for provincial nobles was mandatory, such as the sankin-kotai system of the Tokugawa bakufu.<br /> <br /> That being said, with the way that Third Edition portrays the Great Houses, I actually would be inclined to see them being more widely distributed as a matter of course. I still expect them to regularly travel to and live in the Imperial City for several reasons, not least of which being the need to petition the Scarlet Empress directly (I imagine that trying to communicate with her from afar, let alone make official requests, is outright forbidden), as well as matters pertaining to the Deliberative.<br /> <br /> Really, I'd say that any Dynast with a few decades, a prestigious career, and several children on them is expected to have residences all over the Blessed Isle, and definitely within the top five cities, and regularly travel between them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T05:46:45-08:00","id":1278292,"title":"","content":"Main territory don't have to mean that they spend most of the time there. Most of Roman nobility apparently wanted to be in Rome, even if they owned large pieces of land elsewhere on the peninsula.<br /> <br /> To actually manage said territory, I guess that's what un-exalted Dynasts and Patricians are for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T06:28:24-08:00","id":1278302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1278290#post1278290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't each of the Great Houses have a main territory somewhere on the Blessed Isle?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly something 3rd edition is doing more with.<br /> <br /> For example, in 2nd edition the House of the High Waves a 3 dot Water Manse near Pangu City is &quot;the closest thing that House Cynis has to a major family holding outside the Imperial City&quot; and specifically somewhere they go when they want to get out of sight, with the city itself being little more than an agricultural area and a fishing town that collided.<br /> <br /> In 3rd edition Pangu City is a rather different place &quot;This city, the prefecture\u2019s namesake, houses Cynis scions of all ranks, their courts, their lovers, and their slaves. There\u2019s always some party or another going on in Pangu\u2019s grand houses, and tribute flows through the city like a river. Pangu\u2019s palaces have pleasantly open, airy layouts with rich carpets and sensuous baths, reflecting this love of pleasure and luxury.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T12:38:16-08:00","id":1278381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1278290#post1278290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't each of the Great Houses have a main territory somewhere on the Blessed Isle?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, not to mention the Dragonblooded at the Schools, legions, and working professional jobs like sculpting, those on Safari, and the Fact they Manses in General are homes, and that there are multiple households likely spread across the Continent.<br /> <br /> I can see having estates in the Imperial City, but to live there most of the time that seems odd for 3rd ed. Dragons are out and about doing stuff, even if that stuff is having exotic bachanals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T16:13:50-08:00","id":1278449,"title":"","content":"In thinking back over some of the logistics, I'm reminded of the fact that in addition to the enormous Scarlet Dynasty, the Realm also has a number of native outcastes that <i>also</i> outnumbers the entire Dragon Blooded population of Lookshy. Sure, Lookshy's population of Exalted also consists of a mix of old blood natives and naturalised new blood, but they don't draw so much of a distinction.<br /> <br /> So for the Realm, you probably get a lot of Dynasts who have the luxury of being able to have some personal country estate where they spend a lot of their time drawing on the profits of family business interests or being a noted attendee at all the regional society events or doing something artistic, because the state is able to project its power over vast distances without needing to call upon your service in particular, owing to a vast pool of peasant Exalted for whom military service from the outset is kind of mandatory.<br /> <br /> And sure, part of the reason why the Blessed Isle has such a large number of native outcastes is probably the long term result of their aristocratic setup in the first place. Like, your mother and matriarch will probably gripe and tut over the intemperance of men any time you sow your oats far afield, but at least the Empress would know that doing so is helping to ensure that the mortal population has enough Exalted blood to reliably generate large numbers of people who are so socially disadvantaged that they can't really resist when you say that they've either got to be monks or soldiers, all to the ultimate profit of the Realm and the Dynasty (although the latter complicated a bit by any Dynasts who don't like the idea that they're not as powerful in the military as they think they should be). Or even if it's not as direct as Dragon Blooded men going around having sex with peasant women, there are enough mortal Dynasts with mortal children that eventually they'll descend out of the more privileged strata and carry that bloodline among the plebians, and it's happening all over and has been going for centuries.<br /> <br /> The Scavenger Lands probably has at least as many people overall as the Blessed Isle, but proportionally fewer of them are meaningfully descended from Exalted, and can't become so because Lookshy lacks that reach and rank. And that means that the Dragon Blooded of Lookshy are expected to do more for less.<br /> <br /> Thinking about that brings me to the consideration that, where the Realm is often written as having consistently had ten thousand Dynasts for a reasonably long time, it seems logical that Lookshy has only gotten to 3000 Dragon Blooded fairly recently. I really doubt they had that when they were a Shogunate army left as a garrison force (having taken some losses fighting the Fair Folk? There are later wars, against the Realm and major Eastern invaders, that certainly took their toll), and that would have also created the environment in which they survive primarily by holing up in their fort city and lack the muscle or street cred to turn the mortal population of the region into an engine for continually producing large numbers of Dragon Blooded. At least proportional to the Realm.<br /> <br /> That and how, if proportionally more Gentes Exalted go into military service, their population growth is probably much weaker than the Dynasty's. Sure, most Dynasts don't live past one hundred, but I'll bet you anything that a minority who even make it that far are the ones who dedicated their lives to continuously getting involved in situations with people unreservedly trying to kill them. Lookshy's primary business is not only spreading its Exalted beyond the confines of its walls, it's probably ensuring that a sizable minority of them never come home and procreate.<br /> <br /> One could read Lookshy's state of growing national crisis as being a result of having, after almost eight hundred years, finally started accumulating an Exalted population large enough that they both have the option to expand beyond the traditional model, and might be obligated to if that model is buckling under the strain of them.<br /> <br /> Still, that leaves them with the awkward (and intriguing) question of where their expanding Exalted population is going to go.<br /> <br /> Now, having said all of that... I'm really interested to learn more about Prasad's military. Their Exalted population makes sense for their situation and history, but considering that they're a more actively expansionistic empire neighbouring territorial rivals that can actually put up a decent fight against their mystical strength, it raises a few questions. How large is their military? What proportion of their military are Exalted (and what does having so many of their Exalted out in the wars mean for their society)? Or, in contrast to the Realm and Lookshy, does Prasad need to adapt to its situation by putting less of its Exalted might out in the field, and more into the logistical and organizational side of things? Or is it even just a matter of being uncontested Exalted who reside in splendour and dominate so thoroughly that they can command vast armies of mortals to fight on their behalf, while feeling comfortable making little direct contribution to their success?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T20:41:01-08:00","id":1278494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1278266#post1278266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that depends on what one count as significant, as that is the size of a square with the side of 32 miles, or a circle with a radius of 18 miles. Pretty much everything is at least within one day of forced marching from the city. So pretty much one city, a handful of towns, and a bunch of villages.<br /> <br /> So city-state = a city + the support system to keep it fed and able to defend itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Athens was just the one that was easiest for me to lay hand to a reasonable estimate for, not a particularly big example. The medieval Italian city-states, like Venice or Naples, or maybe classical Carthage, might be better examples. But that said, some estimates put the population around 3-400,000 before the Peloponnesian wars. That puts Athens/Attica at roughly the same size and density as 21st century Luxembourg*. So yeah, small by modern standards, but nothing to sneeze at.<br /> <br /> At any rate, Creation is already wierd, demographically, because it's not really representative of any particular historical period. My point was really just that city-states can still be major regional powers, and that their limited nominal land holdings can be inherently misleading to a moden observer. Most of a larger Bronze/Iron Age country is likely going to be wilderness anyway; somewhere like Lookshy, while nominally small, can be just as influential, powerful, and populated as one with considerably more territory.<br /> <br /> * And numbers are fuzzy but depending what estimate you use that may have been something like 1 out of every 250 extant humans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 01-03-2019, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T22:07:06-08:00","id":1278502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1278449#post1278449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And sure, part of the reason why the Blessed Isle has such a large number of native outcastes is probably the long term result of their aristocratic setup in the first place. Like, your mother and matriarch will probably gripe and tut over the intemperance of men any time you sow your oats far afield, but at least the Empress would know that doing so is helping to ensure that the mortal population has enough Exalted blood to reliably generate large numbers of people who are so socially disadvantaged that they can't really resist when you say that they've either got to be monks or soldiers, all to the ultimate profit of the Realm and the Dynasty (although the latter complicated a bit by any Dynasts who don't like the idea that they're not as powerful in the military as they think they should be). Or even if it's not as direct as Dragon Blooded men going around having sex with peasant women, there are enough mortal Dynasts with mortal children that eventually they'll descend out of the more privileged strata and carry that bloodline among the plebians, and it's happening all over and has been going for centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. In third edition, Lost Eggs are <i>not at all </i>portrayed as the result <i>sowing wild oats</i> (and in fact <i>wasting progenative potential </i>is heavily discouraged). Exaltation among mortals is simply acknowledged as a thing that happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 01-04-2019, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T23:35:45-08:00","id":1278507,"title":"","content":"Just because something is discouraged doesn't mean it doesn't happen. Moreover, the progenitive potential is only &quot;wasted&quot; if you're expected to try and father a child for the Realm sometime within the next ten years, which, if you're a soldier in the Legions or a Dynast engaging in adventure-tourism in the Threshold, may not be all that likely.<br /> <br /> If you're married and trying to raise a family on the Blessed Isle, yes, those indiscretions are going to be stigmatized. If you're a career soldier going putting down rebellions from satrapy to satrapy, one whose likelihood of even returning to the Realm proper alive <i>at all</i> - let alone within the next ten years - is a coin-flip, they're not going to care as such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-04-2019, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T00:51:26-08:00","id":1278515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1278502#post1278502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. In third edition, Lost Eggs are <i>not at all </i>portrayed as the result <i>sowing wild oats</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that's technically accurate, but I'm using it as an idiom because it's an idiom for the thing that I'm taking about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (and in fact <i>wasting progenative potential </i>is heavily discouraged)</div> </div> </div> </div>It is?! You mean, like, their wives and mothers and matriarchs gripe and tut over the intemperance of men? That's news to me!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exaltation among mortals is simply acknowledged as a thing that happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall that being the way that the book portrays it, and I'm quite certain that's not how it works in the setting. It's Terrestrial Exaltation; it paradigmatically functions as a result of heredity. Thin-blooded are not generated spontaneously, they are the result of the tiniest trickle of the Dragon's blood enduring until the point where it blossoms into Exaltation.<br /> <br /> Which can happen as a result of Exalted having children with mortals of no bloodline, or from the mortal descendants of even two Terrestrials (the latter possibility I also mentioned, that you've disregarded completely).<br /> <br /> It's hardly a coincidence that the Isle where the Dragon Blooded reign supreme gives rise to so many outcastes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T06:26:39-08:00","id":1279181,"title":"","content":"I think the commingling of the Dragons' blood with humanity's is less a result of Dynastic indiscretion and more a result of the many thousands of years of history <i>prior</i> to the Dynasty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T07:09:18-08:00","id":1279196,"title":"","content":"Well, a Dragon-Blood and a mortal is probably a lot more likely to provide a Dragon-Blooded offspring, than two mortals having a Dragon-Blooded ancestor some 10-15 generations back. With the sheer number of the second category, I think it falls well within &quot;scholars can't agree on the issue&quot;, where in-game beliefs and facts might not match, and an official canon would be silly considering how Ex3 is said to stay clear of nailing down things as 2nd ed did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T08:11:35-08:00","id":1279213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279181#post1279181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the commingling of the Dragons' blood with humanity's is less a result of Dynastic indiscretion and more a result of the many thousands of years of history <i>prior</i> to the Dynasty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's primarily going to be a result of not every person with Dragon blood Exalting, and not as many of their own children, and after two or three generations they get married off into the patricians, and can ultimately descend lower.<br /> <br /> There has to be something that distinguishes the Blessed Isle from the rest of the world in how many outcastes pop up, and being home to the Scarlet Dynasty seems like a good start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T08:17:22-08:00","id":1279216,"title":"","content":"Well, that depends if you assume that originally dragonblooded had a 100% exaltation rate in their kids as long as they stuck to dragon/dragon pairs. <br /> <br /> In that case the first &quot;mortal&quot; blood probably came from celestial exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T08:30:20-08:00","id":1279220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279216#post1279216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that depends if you assume that originally dragonblooded had a 100% exaltation rate in their kids as long as they stuck to dragon/dragon pairs. <br /> <br /> In that case the first &amp;quot;mortal&amp;quot; blood probably came from celestial exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we know this to be true, what with generative essence.<br /> <br /> But I believe Exalts and Gods don\u2019t dilute the blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T09:34:58-08:00","id":1279237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279216#post1279216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that depends if you assume that originally dragonblooded had a 100% exaltation rate in their kids as long as they stuck to dragon/dragon pairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's been thrown out. I know the original 10,000 Dragon-Blooded who created the army of the gods via a giant orgy, are gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T10:24:38-08:00","id":1279246,"title":"","content":"Actually thinking about it the first generation probably had a fair few mortal spouses. <br /> <br /> So even if that could have theoretically been true, it's possible that it never happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T10:24:49-08:00","id":1279247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279213#post1279213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, it's primarily going to be a result of not every person with Dragon blood Exalting, and not as many of their own children, and after two or three generations they get married off into the patricians, and can ultimately descend lower.</div> </div> </div> </div>There have been big dragon-blooded families on the Blessed Isle since long before the Dynasty, and even long before the Shogunate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There has to be something that distinguishes the Blessed Isle from the rest of the world in how many outcastes pop up, and being home to the Scarlet Dynasty seems like a good start. </div> </div> </div>It is not clear to me that outcastes are disproportionately born on the Blessed Isle. WFHL is, as far as I can recall, silent on this. The Realm has so many outcastes (at least in part) because it attracts many foreign ones too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T10:26:12-08:00","id":1279248,"title":"","content":"There are more Dynastic outcastes than lookshyans, but slightly less than there are miscellaneous foreign outcastes.<br /> <br /> It's in a census on page 18","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T10:39:49-08:00","id":1279252,"title":"","content":"Yes but the Dynastic outcastes include foreigners who joined the Realm, or at least that's my understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T11:41:49-08:00","id":1279264,"title":"","content":"I think there is some strong arguing past each other here. DB Exaltation is passed down via blood, and we even have rough numbers on what that looks like from the book. This does mean that because of the concentration of DB families on the Blessed Isle for so many years is part of the explanation, but we also know that the Scarlet Empress was actively working to ensure there were as many DBs as possible, since they are a crucial part of growing, expanding and maintaining the empire. Long history of DB blood + active policies to ensure higher chances of exaltation are going to result in the best chance of having the grist for the mill of exalted imperialism. None of which really contradicts or argues against Isator Levi's points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23811-taintedbalance","name":"TaintedBalance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23811_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T11:57:34-08:00","id":1279273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279252#post1279252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes but the Dynastic outcastes include foreigners who joined the Realm, or at least that's my understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's correct. However, foreigners constitute a minuscule fraction of that number. Few foreign outcastes wish to surrender their freedom and independence in order to join the Imperial legions or the Immaculate Order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T12:50:15-08:00","id":1279287,"title":"","content":"Thank you for clarifying, Eric.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T13:19:26-08:00","id":1279290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279237#post1279237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's been thrown out. I know the original 10,000 Dragon-Blooded who created the army of the gods via a giant orgy, are gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait what the Prehistoric Orgy is gone too? What?! Was their still 10k of them st first?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T13:22:59-08:00","id":1279292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279290#post1279290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait what the Prehistoric Orgy is gone too? What?!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, dead as a doornail.<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;We need to cast down the enemies of the gods; for that, we'll need an army!&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;Well, we <i>just made</i> an army. They can-&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;Good idea! Let's have the army literally <i>go fuck itself</i>, and their offspring can be the army we'll use!&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;Won't that delay the war efforts by at least an entire generation, and shit all over the people we <i>just</i>\u200b got through telling they were heroes worthy of our power and legacy? Is it even necessary to implement this breeding program? How are ten thousand demigod heroes not <i>enough</i>?&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;Meh.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bSo, um, yeah, good riddance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279290#post1279290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was their still 10k of them st first?</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it matter? (No, it doesn't.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-07-2019, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T13:33:09-08:00","id":1279294,"title":"","content":"Yeah cool it still makes a difference. Even Solars had Casualties so startin with only 10k Dragonblooded is a good way for them to go extinct.<br /> <br /> Hence it\u2019s a big change if they started with say a 100k or a million. Law of Dimishment and all they rot...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T13:42:23-08:00","id":1279296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279294#post1279294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah cool it still makes a difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your argument is hardly convincing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279294#post1279294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even Solars had Casualties so startin with only 10k Dragonblooded is a good way for them to go extinct.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the power boost Dragon-Blooded have gotten, I wouldn't count them out so quickly.<br /> <br /> (Just gonna ignore the &quot;Even Solars had casualties&quot; bit for the irrelevant tangent it is...)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279294#post1279294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hence it\u2019s a big change if they started with say a 100k or a million. Law of Dimishment and all they rot...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying the number literally doesn't matter, because <i>whatever the number is</i>, be it ten thousand or a million or just one thousand, it's an unimportant detail. The important detail is that the Dragons empowered the greatest mortals they could find to be an army to cast down the enemies of the gods, and from the loins of those heroes was born a race of demigods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T13:51:45-08:00","id":1279297,"title":"","content":"What\u2019s important is debatable. You could say nothing is important so stop discussing it, and that is not st all helpful.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m very willing and to be sold on this idea but several Exalted forum members seem to jump on new changes mentioned in a thread not everyone has read and seem to act like it\u2019s in the books already. People immediately act like it\u2019s super obvious and poopoo when people haven\u2019t heard of it yet. I get it\u2019s fun to d*ckride everything the devs say but outside you introducing the \u201cnews\u201d you aren\u2019t being very helpful crapping on people not immediatly stepping in line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T14:03:01-08:00","id":1279300,"title":"","content":"I'm not crapping on people; I'm calling out problematic, shitty writing, which the prehistoric orgy <i>absolutely</i> was.<br /> <br /> \u200bI haven't been a fan of this particular snippet of the setting <i>long</i> before the devs indicated it was being banished, so please don't treat me like it was Vance and Minton's decision to excise it that made me so against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-07-2019, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T14:06:58-08:00","id":1279301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279300#post1279300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...shitty writing...</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a matter of opinion and taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T14:14:18-08:00","id":1279303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279301#post1279301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a matter of opinion and taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>That some people have a taste for shit doesn't change that they're eating shit. The notion that the Dragon-Blooded were insufficient to handle the challenge <i>they were empowered for in the first place</i> and had to shore up their weakness by engaging in a multigenerational orgy that just happened to resemble the misogynistic red-pill basement-troll's vision of heaven, where each man got 99 women to make babies for him (and conveniently neglects to bring up all the inherent problems with that)? <b>That. Is. Shit.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-07-2019, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T14:23:10-08:00","id":1279304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279303#post1279303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That some people have a taste for shit doesn't change that they're eating shit. The notion that the Dragon-Blooded were insufficient to handle the challenge <i>they were empowered for in the first place</i> and had to shore up their weakness by engaging in a multigenerational orgy that just happened to resemble the misogynistic red-pill basement-troll's vision of heaven, where each man got 99 women to make babies for him? <b>That. Is. Shit.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>For those wanting the gods to exalt mortals out of their love of humans, yeah, the old writing don't work well.<br /> <br /> But where they just were tools for an end, and having limited resources (the setting lacks omnipotence after all) having them use humans as cattle kind of fit. And being designated stud in a breeding program probably won't be that much of heaven (well, it still can be a dream, as nightmares after all also per definition are dreams).<br /> <br /> Out of respect for this site, I won't answer the rest of your post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T17:24:23-08:00","id":1279345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279297#post1279297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get it\u2019s fun to d*ckride everything the devs say</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Well that's pretty rude and some rather homophobic imagery you're going with there!<br /> <br /> I think the worst part about this is that you've been part of this community for years and seen how people would reference things that Moran, Neph or Grabowski had said on internet forums as statements of authoral intent, we've been collectively 'dickriding' various writers for years it's just now you choose to assign something vulgar to it. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T19:02:24-08:00","id":1279367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279290#post1279290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait what the Prehistoric Orgy is gone too? What?! Was their still 10k of them st first?</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything about the Dragon-Blooded that reads like it was made up by a 19th century eugenicist instead of by epic myth storytellers is thankfully gone, yes.<br /> <br /> 3rd Edition treats them as epic heroes with agency. No breeding camps allowed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T19:06:19-08:00","id":1279368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279294#post1279294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah cool it still makes a difference. Even Solars had Casualties so startin with only 10k Dragonblooded is a good way for them to go extinct.<br /> <br /> Hence it\u2019s a big change if they started with say a 100k or a million. Law of Dimishment and all they rot...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Minutia about the mechanics of the creation of the Dragon-Blooded add absolutely nothing to the setting by being defined, while shrouding it in legend at least provides atmospheric texture to the setting. What possible value could be derived from nailing down their exact starting number and reproductive strategies from over 5,000 years ago, and removing myths in the process?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T19:15:41-08:00","id":1279371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279304#post1279304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those wanting the gods to exalt mortals out of their love of humans, yeah, the old writing don't work well.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not about the gods. Is whether Dragon Blooded themselves have individual heroic agency or if the setting treats them like mass bred mooks. As you said, breeding camps would be horrific. Thousands of Exalted forced into them could never be contained! They\u2019d immediately rebel against the cruelty of the gods trying to treat them like cattle, as being Exalted they easily have the power to do so!<br /> <br /> <br /> This being one of the most hated parts of 2E is not new information. It\u2019s been widely and consistently derided since CoCD: the Blessed Isle was first published. Unfortunately one particular 2E writer had a thing for breeding camps (not any of the ones who have had a forum presence in the past).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T19:23:33-08:00","id":1279374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279345#post1279345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Well that's pretty rude and some rather homophobic imagery you're going with there!<br /> <br /> I think the worst part about this is that you've been part of this community for years and seen how people would reference things that Moran, Neph or Grabowski had said on internet forums as statements of authoral intent, we've been collectively 'dickriding' various writers for years it's just now you choose to assign something vulgar to it. </b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ll apologize if it\u2019s construed as something homophobic. I\u2019m used to it being used as a cheeky way of saying sucking up or kissing which itself has very obvious imagery, that\u2019s used by males and females concerning males and females.I bleeped out a naughty word, but by itself I didn\u2019t mean harm as I even included myself when I said I get it\u2019s fun to BLANK.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I\u2019m pointing out is one shouldn\u2019t take Changes to the setting and say it\u2019s super obvious and that should have always been the case. Of course there are Black Swans in Australia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T20:23:55-08:00","id":1279381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279368#post1279368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Minutia about the mechanics of the creation of the Dragon-Blooded add absolutely nothing to the setting by being defined, while shrouding it in legend at least provides atmospheric texture to the setting. What possible value could be derived from nailing down their exact starting number and reproductive strategies from over 5,000 years ago, and removing myths in the process?</div> </div> </div> </div>We aren\u2019t even talking about minutia, we are talking about how many Dragonblooded were first Exalted.<br /> <br /> Minutia would be talking about exact numbers. But it makes a difference if the Celestial Exalted lead an Army of 1k, 10k, 100k or a million. We don\u2019t need the answers but the discussion is relavent. <br /> <br /> What is wrong with discussing it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T20:31:05-08:00","id":1279383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279303#post1279303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That some people have a taste for shit doesn't change that they're eating shit. The notion that the Dragon-Blooded were insufficient to handle the challenge <i>they were empowered for in the first place</i> and had to shore up their weakness by engaging in a multigenerational orgy that just happened to resemble the misogynistic red-pill basement-troll's vision of heaven, where each man got 99 women to make babies for him (and conveniently neglects to bring up all the inherent problems with that)? <b>That. Is. Shit.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>See how it okay to say other people have a taste for poo? And to say subjectively your opinions and sensibilities are poo. This doesn\u2019t even warrant a reprimand. Is it because I don\u2019t flag/report things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T21:59:13-08:00","id":1279398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279381#post1279381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We aren\u2019t even talking about minutia, we are talking about how many Dragonblooded were first Exalted.<br /> <br /> Minutia would be talking about exact numbers. But it makes a difference if the Celestial Exalted lead an Army of 1k, 10k, 100k or a million. We don\u2019t need the answers but the discussion is relavent. <br /> <br /> What is wrong with discussing it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Discussing it on the forums? Nothing.<br /> <br /> Nailing it down in canon which is what I was talking about<b></b>: it has no impact on the setting whatsoever as it currently exists in RY 768, hence it being irrelevant minutia. It provides more plot hooks and inspiration as the subject of vague myths than given a canonical answer.<br /> <br /> And I cannot stress this point enough - especially doesn\u2019t add anything positive to the setting with canonical eugenic mass breeding that completely undermines the agency of individual Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T23:46:41-08:00","id":1279410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279383#post1279383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to say subjectively your opinions and sensibilities are poo. This doesn\u2019t even warrant a reprimand.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because I didn't say your opinions or sensibilities are poo. I said the writing was poo. And you can like poo, but you <i>should</i> be aware that it is poo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279383#post1279383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it because I don\u2019t flag/report things?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you feel I've crossed the line, please don't hesitate to report me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T01:23:58-08:00","id":1279420,"title":"","content":"Aaand the forum isn't working properly on my laptop again. Fine; I guess we're doing this the long way.<br /> <br /> Actually... no, that stretches even my patience. Any time your quotes look short, just assume that I'm responding to a wider point around them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">dragonblooded had a 100% exaltation rate</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually assume that they did only for the very first born generation of them, but that they otherwise worked no differently to how the book describes their general heredity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalts and Gods don't dilute the blood</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have no progenitive Essence, the child has lower odds of Exalting. Gods and Exalted of the wrong parentage can dilute the blood more than having a child with the right mortal can.<br /> <br /> Nobody forget that odds of Exaltation can be the highest it is possible to be, and still fail. That does leave you with a mortal with very high chances of producing an Exalted child.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">fair few mortal spouses</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean consecutively? Because simultaneously, it would only be functional for men, and with progenitive Essence it wouldn't be functional at all.<br /> <br /> Really, that's the biggest reason why the absence of a mythic orgy should be taken as a given; it plain doesn't work anymore.<br /> <br /> Mind, in the past, I've pointed out ways in which it never actually worked as written if you stopped to think about it for a second. I mean, wouldn't every woman have become pregnant really quickly, and then the sex can stop for a year?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TaintedBalance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">actively working to ensure there were as many DBs</div> </div> </div> </div>Albeit counterbalanced a bit by things like stipend policies and the wars. Too many Exalted makes her reign more unstable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">startin with only 10k Dragonblooded is a good way for them to go extinct</div> </div> </div> </div>Leaving aside the begged question, there's a middle ground between the first group of them going straight into battle without growing their numbers and securing their legacy, and needing to increase numbers rapidly through constant group sex (which I'm going to reiterate would not help anyway, in either Edition).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T01:45:21-08:00","id":1279422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279371#post1279371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s not about the gods. Is whether Dragon Blooded themselves have individual heroic agency or if the setting treats them like mass bred mooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what? You're saying their origin story would make or break their ability to be heroic?!?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As you said, breeding camps would be horrific. Thousands of Exalted forced into them could never be contained! They\u2019d immediately rebel against the cruelty of the gods trying to treat them like cattle, as being Exalted they easily have the power to do so! </div> </div> </div>Both elementals, and seeds of nature (they are tracing their lineage to Gaia after all), tend to start small and grow. So it might have taken a while for the power to mature. Also, a 100:1 ratio would mean if the gods would manage to sell the idea to 5-20% of women, and such rebellion would most likely be squashed within their own ranks,<br /> <br /> Second edition have after all a quite larger power discrepancy between terrestrial and celestial exalts, On the Cosmic scale, they were bacteria or small ants boosted up to bull ants; still insignificant individually, but dangerous if swarmed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This being one of the most hated parts of 2E is not new information. It\u2019s been widely and consistently derided since CoCD: the Blessed Isle was first published. Unfortunately one particular 2E writer had a thing for breeding camps (not any of the ones who have had a forum presence in the past). </div> </div> </div>And Ex3 have a completely new approach. So those that hated it don't have to bother with it anymore. Great. It's still a matter of taste, and taking a piss on an earlier edition (which nine times out of ten is pissing on the fanon but blaming the books, not what's actually written) is nothing but edition warring. <br /> <br /> Pointing out that 2nd ed at times had shit writings, because while it is very clear to me what they wanted to say in the infamous &quot;Homosexuality Versus Effeminacy&quot; sidebar, it was expressed in a way I would count as tone deaf even at the time it was printed.<br /> <br /> Letting a writer with a thing for breeding camps write without oversight means text not fitting most peoples taste. It's still just taste. I don't mind at all that a lot/most/all say they didn't like what 2nd ed did and love where Ex3 is taking things. That's just expressing ones own preference. Going on how some are about second edition, not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T01:53:13-08:00","id":1279428,"title":"","content":"Just gonna sidestep this...<br /> <br /> So I wonder what form a Lookshy that is newly expansionist because their numbers have grown beyond their current boundaries might look like.<br /> <br /> I had an image of it being coupled with their other modern concerns, in which war against Thorns kind of evolves into continuous expansion south, possibly over the Mnemon satrapies.<br /> <br /> Mind, that still leaves a question of whether the rest of the Confederation will tolerate such unilateral action, even if they're not the targets of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T02:38:42-08:00","id":1279436,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I meant that since the first generation of deebs were exalted as adults ex-nihilo, it's reasonable to assume some of them already had partners at the time. Some might even have had kids.<br /> <br /> ...Do you think progenitive essence works retroactively?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T03:08:20-08:00","id":1279439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279436#post1279436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I meant that since the first generation of deebs were exalted as adults ex-nihilo, it's reasonable to assume some of them already had partners at the time. Some might even have had kids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah; that makes a lot more sense.<br /> <br /> I see no reason to assume not, although my conception of humanity of the time would be that they didn't have marriage as such, and my conception of the origin of the Terrestrial Exalted is that if you were somebody that actually made it with your life partner to stand before the Elemental Dragons, you were uplifted (and if you weren't, you either died on the journey or drifted back to do something different with your life). Either way, the process of even reaching them entailed and required forging strong bonds of community.<br /> <br /> I envision many more being called than those who made it all the way.<br /> <br /> I also see them including gay and non-binary people, who were afforded special dispensations by the grace of the Dragons for their very first generation. Like, you wouldn't need the assistance of a sorcerer for your dream conceptions and babies out of the cabbage patch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Do you think progenitive essence works retroactively?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, although for every generation after the first you do still have it before you Exalt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T03:16:17-08:00","id":1279441,"title":"","content":"You're describing a much more involved exaltation process to what I was imagining.<br /> <br /> I thought it was just a celestial style &quot;Boom, fire powers&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T04:07:56-08:00","id":1279448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You're describing a much more involved exaltation process to what I was imagining.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I thought it was just a celestial style &quot;Boom, fire powers&quot;</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Well, first I'm mostly thinking in terms of the kinds of legends that the Dragon Blooded would have told amongst themselves*. From that, I think there would need to be something referencing the idea that they view the Caul as the place where they originated (and really, it kind of ought to be).<br /> <br /> Then I'm thinking that considering various aspects of the Dragon Blooded, such as the draw to kinship and the power benefits and the fact that pairing amongst themselves helps their Exaltation to propagate, it helps to have all of them together when they start out (even if my image of their origins has them quickly divide into smaller groups and spread across the world, rather than stay clumped as a single target).<br /> <br /> And finally, since it would be the one and only time when a bunch of people became Terrestrial Exalted in a manner other than inheriting it from ancestors, I think it deserves a bit of mythic oomph. <br /> <br /> * Although my main conception of the difference between narrative and reality is in the character ascribed to the Five Elemental Dragons.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T07:26:40-08:00","id":1279463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279422#post1279422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, what? You're saying their origin story would make or break their ability to be heroic?!?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of the individual player character, not necessarily. But if the setting is trying to communicate \u201cthese are elemental demigods, in whose veins course the power of the pillars of the world itself\u201d it absolutely fails by treating them like a mass breeding program. How you write the setting communicates the game\u2019s themes. It makes being an epic hero playing against type for a Dragon Blooded instead of there inherent nature as it should be for all Exalted (in vastly different ways).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T07:42:28-08:00","id":1279466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279463#post1279463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of the individual player character, not necessarily. But if the setting is trying to communicate \u201cthese are elemental demigods, in whose veins course the power of the pillars of the world itself\u201d it absolutely fails by treating them like a mass breeding program. How you write the setting communicates the game\u2019s themes. It makes being an epic hero playing against type for a Dragon Blooded instead of there inherent nature as it should be for all Exalted (in vastly different ways).</div> </div> </div> </div>Or being the epic heroes that rose above what they where created to be.<br /> <br /> It might not be the kind of epic heroes you want them to be, but as I say, that's a matter of preference and Ex3 have a different solution (I don't even know what 1st ed went with) that seems to fit most on this site anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T09:23:26-08:00","id":1279484,"title":"","content":"I mean, you have to assume the Elemental Dragons ran the numbers and exalted enough people that they were confident that enough would survive fighting to produce the next generation. <br /> <br /> Apparently that was about 10,000. If you think it would need to be more, assume they exalted more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T10:06:01-08:00","id":1279491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279484#post1279484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, you have to assume the Elemental Dragons ran the numbers and exalted enough people that they were confident that enough would survive fighting to produce the next generation. <br /> <br /> Apparently that was about 10,000. If you think it would need to be more, assume they exalted more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess a big question is how many Dragonblooded were around right after the War. Did they kill literally Billions if Enemies without getting decimated. Did the Dragonblooded start the Age of Man with strong numbers or did they have to cultivate them for centuries?<br /> <br /> And I\u2019m still under the Assumption there were over a million Dragonblooded during the Usurpation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T10:09:51-08:00","id":1279492,"title":"","content":"Well, it is also worth noting that ten thousand (\u4e07) in some Asian cultures also apparently is used for &quot;a very large number&quot; and not only that specific amount.<br /> <br /> As Exalted takes a lot of inspiration from there, saying that they created ten thousand could mean it was 53,817 that was Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T10:13:30-08:00","id":1279495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279492#post1279492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it is also worth noting that ten thousand (\u4e07) in some Asian cultures also apparently is used for &amp;quot;a very large number&amp;quot; and not only that specific amount.<br /> <br /> As Exalted takes a lot of inspiration from there, saying that they created ten thousand could mean it was 53,817 that was Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it\u2019s often a placeholder for infinite.<br /> <br /> <br /> So it seems 3rd ed approaches the idea that what it\u2019s possible Dragonblooded were officers in Armies of Mortals rather then pure Exalt Armies with Dragonking and Mountainfolk auxiliaries?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T10:21:22-08:00","id":1279497,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Myriad Dragons&quot; would be how to say it in English.<br /> <br /> Myriad means literally &quot;ten thousand&quot; but metaphorically &quot;a fuckload&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T10:23:45-08:00","id":1279498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279491#post1279491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess a big question is how many Dragonblooded were around right after the War. Did they kill literally Billions if Enemies without getting decimated. Did the Dragonblooded start the Age of Man with strong numbers or did they have to cultivate them for centuries?<br /> <br /> And I\u2019m still under the Assumption there were over a million Dragonblooded during the Usurpation.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we are still talking about 3,500 years from the end of the Primordial war to the Usurpation, they could have come out of the war with just a few thousand, and still easily be a million by then.<br /> <br /> For comparison, here is a list over the population growth of the real world. <a href=\"http://www.worldometers.info/world-population/world-population-by-year/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.worldometers.info/world-p...ation-by-year/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T10:44:33-08:00","id":1279501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279498#post1279498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we are still talking about 3,500 years from the end of the Primordial war to the Usurpation, they could have come out of the war with just a few thousand, and still easily be a million by then.<br /> <br /> For comparison, here is a list over the population growth of the real world. <a href=\"http://www.worldometers.info/world-population/world-population-by-year/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.worldometers.info/world-p...ation-by-year/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I believe it.<br /> <br /> But real population growth doesn\u2019t mesh well with how Dragons breed true.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also if one doesn\u2019t care about cultivating their generative essence can\u2019t they just still breed a huge brood of dragon touched, and purebred dragon touched if they have a strong bloodline and keep a host of strong blooded mates?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T11:16:21-08:00","id":1279507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279501#post1279501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also if one doesn\u2019t care about cultivating their generative essence can\u2019t they just still breed a huge brood of dragon touched, and purebred dragon touched if they have a strong bloodline and keep a host of strong blooded mates?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hard to parse your question, because your terminology doesn't match the book's.<br /> <br /> I'm gonna say that creating as many children as you can with a microscopic bloodline is not preferable to the odds you get if you wait and have a child with the best partner you can find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T11:35:50-08:00","id":1279517,"title":"","content":"I think he's been reading Holden's crossover book. <br /> <br /> But as far as large broods of mortals go, bear in mind that the entirety of mortal creation combined produces about as many dragon blooded as the dynasty does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T11:44:53-08:00","id":1279519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279501#post1279501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh I believe it.<br /> <br /> But real population growth doesn\u2019t mesh well with how Dragons breed true.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also if one doesn\u2019t care about cultivating their generative essence can\u2019t they just still breed a huge brood of dragon touched, and purebred dragon touched if they have a strong bloodline and keep a host of strong blooded mates?</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of progenitive essence is, in short, that there isn't such a thing as 'DB breeding optimization tactics' anymore. That's the thing that changed. Strategically yes, you should have <i>at least</i> one baby every so many years or you're wasting potential. But I think it's apparent that within the limits of typical behaviour, any given parent can expect roughly the same number of DB children per unit time, averaged out with their mate(s). There's no particular advantage, immediately or over the long haul, to the DB population for being a K strategists vs M strategists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T11:55:37-08:00","id":1279525,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not even talking about having your own kids be Dragonblooded, but I am talking about if you made a bunch of kids because say you didn\u2019t care, would these same offspring be as desirable as Mates for Dragonblooded if they were cultivated carefully but didn\u2019t breed true out of luck?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T13:24:51-08:00","id":1279554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279525#post1279525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not even talking about having your own kids be Dragonblooded, but I am talking about if you made a bunch of kids because say you didn\u2019t care, would these same offspring be as desirable as Mates for Dragonblooded if they were cultivated carefully but didn\u2019t breed true out of luck?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they'd be godawful.<br /> <br /> Inheriting Exaltation isn't about breeding true; if your parents maximize progenitive Essence, you definitely get that, but it might not become Exaltation, even if their bloodlines are immaculate. That high quality Essence/bloodline can pass to further children.<br /> <br /> If they have children when their Essence is spent, those children inherit barely anything, and what they pass down will be equally insignificant. Even if the parents are well-bred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T14:32:16-08:00","id":1279564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279501#post1279501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also if one doesn\u2019t care about cultivating their generative essence can\u2019t they just still breed a huge brood of dragon touched, and purebred dragon touched if they have a strong bloodline and keep a host of strong blooded mates?</div> </div> </div> </div> Dragon Touched, as in the Terrestrial Half-Caste that 2e retconned from existence?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T14:39:50-08:00","id":1279568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1278291#post1278291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still expect them to regularly travel to and live in the Imperial City for several reasons, not least of which being the need to petition the Scarlet Empress directly (I imagine that trying to communicate with her from afar, let alone make official requests, is outright forbidden), as well as matters pertaining to the Deliberative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine the punishment for bothering the Empress with unsolicited Infallible Messengers starts at financial ruin and complete social ostracism for you personally and only goes up from there depending on how annoying you were about it. Though given how many foreign sorcerers who believe they are reasonably beyond reprisal for it there are (even if just young, stupid graduate of Lookshy's Academy of Sorcery) she probably had some artifact or working done centuries ago to intercept her calls with important people being appointed to actually be there to receive them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T15:15:21-08:00","id":1279573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279525#post1279525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not even talking about having your own kids be Dragonblooded, but I am talking about if you made a bunch of kids because say you didn\u2019t care, would these same offspring be as desirable as Mates for Dragonblooded if they were cultivated carefully but didn\u2019t breed true out of luck?</div> </div> </div> </div>So if you assume I'm right about <i>why</i> progentive essence exists (&quot;<i>The point of progenitive essence is, in short, that there isn't such a thing as 'DB breeding optimization tactics' anymore.</i>&quot; - me) then the answer is no. In order to make sense in that context, your children's Breeding, like their Exaltation rate, would have to <i>also</i> be a function of your progenitive essence at the time of conception. They can't be (fully) independent.<br /> <br /> Which, honestly, kind of makes sense. Something like, Breeding is a static property, set at your conception, that sets your exaltation chance as well as your progenitive essence &quot;cap&quot; and &quot;recharge rate&quot;, and is based on the strength of your parent's progenitive essence at the time of conception. So, low-Breeding parents still have low-Breeding kids (because their essence only ever gets so strong), but high-Breeding parents can also have low-Breeding kids (if they make babies faster than their essence recharges).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 01-08-2019, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T15:22:41-08:00","id":1279574,"title":"","content":"My reasoning is that forcing them to present petitions in person reinforces the mystique of the monarchy, limits the flow of requests, and makes it just inconvenient enough to dissuade some.<br /> <br /> I don't think punishment for trying need be particularly extreme. It actually seems like something where being reprimanded and humiliated in public could get the job done.<br /> <br /> Really, given the setting's leaning on larger than life relationships, I think that a lot can come from verbally castigating another person. Not all attacks need to be physical or material.<br /> <br /> Just imagine what that would be like for a Dynast, forced to present yourself before her Majesty and plant your face on the ground while she lacerated you for daring to address her from afar, while surrounded by your peers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T15:23:35-08:00","id":1279575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279568#post1279568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine the punishment for bothering the Empress with unsolicited Infallible Messengers starts at financial ruin and complete social ostracism for you personally and only goes up from there depending on how annoying you were about it. Though given how many foreign sorcerers who believe they are reasonably beyond reprisal for it there are (even if just young, stupid graduate of Lookshy's Academy of Sorcery) she probably had some artifact or working done centuries ago to intercept her calls with important people being appointed to actually be there to receive them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you need to <i>name</i> your target?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T15:42:11-08:00","id":1279581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279574#post1279574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My reasoning is that forcing them to present petitions in person reinforces the mystique of the monarchy, limits the flow of requests, and makes it just inconvenient enough to dissuade some.<br /> <br /> I don't think punishment for trying need be particularly extreme. It actually seems like something where being reprimanded and humiliated in public could get the job done.<br /> <br /> Really, given the setting's leaning on larger than life relationships, I think that a lot can come from verbally castigating another person. Not all attacks need to be physical or material.<br /> <br /> Just imagine what that would be like for a Dynast, forced to present yourself before her Majesty and plant your face on the ground while she lacerated you for daring to address her from afar, while surrounded by your peers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was attempting to be a little cheeky, but upon rereading that just made it unclear. I meant that the automatic level of consequences would be financial ruin and social ostracism. In my mind, having drawn the personal ire of the Empress in that way would tend to naturally lead to the family making a show of cutting your stipend, all the party invitations drying up because no one wants to be associated with you, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> The &quot;goes up from there&quot; part was anything the Empress did to punish you if, for example, you made vulgar remarks in the message itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279575#post1279575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't you need to <i>name</i> your target?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, not according to 3E anyway. The spell only mentions &quot;another character&quot; and the &quot;intended target&quot;. Sorcerers with it as their control spell can project their senses through it. Being able to observe the Empress' doings seems like too big a security risk to allow even beyond the distraction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T16:32:13-08:00","id":1279590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279564#post1279564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Dragon Touched, as in the Terrestrial Half-Caste that 2e retconned from existence?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean them more to represent humans that can have Dragonblooded kids, like Kinfolk for the Garou. Like Dynasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T16:43:07-08:00","id":1279595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279554#post1279554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they have children when their Essence is spent, those children inherit barely anything, and what they pass down will be equally insignificant. Even if the parents are well-bred.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that this specifically is not correct in 3E (note that I'm on the same page as you otherwise). On page 98 they specifically mention for having back to back kids, the 'leftover children', that &quot;Even if she Exalts, the stigma remains to a lesser extent, with her bloodline baselesly considered inferior to that of her more esteemed kin.&quot; They then follow up saying that mortals always have the same chance, no matter what. From this information we can deduce that the Exalt's bloodline is the only variable factor going on here (it does say anything about if you say took two mortals from an otherwise peerless bloodline, and they had a child who Exalted and what that Exalts bloodline would look like). <br /> <br /> A quick reading of the paragraph following that could also be a source of confusion, since it notes that the progenitive potency passes on at conception, but only completely drains the parents. Honestly re-reading the section a couple times now, it's a bit vague, but with that quote above about the bloodline being diminished as baseless, I lean towards what is passed down is always same, as long as you Exalt to enjoy the benefit. I'll bow my head if the devs have addressed it specifically elsewhere, although for my game I prefer this interpretation. Having large swaths of common sense/knowledge being dead wrong adds to the world for me!<br /> <br /> As an aside, I worked out a calculator for chance to Exalt DB based on all the various information given and with the following assumptions you get a bit more than a doubling of DB potential every 2 generations (this is actually really slow population growth compared to say humans, and i say potential because some might not have exalted yet when that generation marker passes):<br /> <br /> A generation happens every 12 years (pg 99, 12-20 years for maximum chance)<br /> The progenitive curve is sigmoidal<br /> Strong bloodline is 1.6x more likely than baseline to exalt and compose 25% of DBs<br /> Weak bloodline is 0.4x less likely than baseline to exalt and compose 25% of DBs<br /> <br /> The above analysis is kind of rosey, and I would personally whack it down to a 1.5x increase of the DB population ever 2 &quot;generations&quot; to take into account things like sleeping around too much, early deaths, etc etc. But even with that, within ~150 years you'd go from 10k DB to ~113k DB. It is not at all unreasonable that there were literally millions of DB when the great contagion came around and killed almost everyone, followed by the Fae Invasion. <br /> <br /> As a final note, please only do math like this if its actually important to some point or part of your story. The best answer for how many DB there are is &quot;as many as are needed for your group's story to work&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23811-taintedbalance","name":"TaintedBalance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23811_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T01:47:32-08:00","id":1279658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TaintedBalance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279595#post1279595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe that this specifically is not correct in 3E (note that I'm on the same page as you otherwise). On page 98 they specifically mention for having back to back kids, the 'leftover children', that &amp;quot;Even if she Exalts, the stigma remains to a lesser extent, with her bloodline baselesly considered inferior to that of her more esteemed kin.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. They added in a word from the version we got in the Kickstarter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-Lez_WdX70c\" data-code=\"-Lez_WdX70c\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/-Lez_WdX70c/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TaintedBalance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A quick reading of the paragraph following that could also be a source of confusion, since it notes that the progenitive potency passes on at conception, but only completely drains the parents. Honestly re-reading the section a couple times now, it's a bit vague, but with that quote above about the bloodline being diminished as baseless, I lean towards what is passed down is always same, as long as you Exalt to enjoy the benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there's also still the sidebar at the beginning of chapter 2 that says how bloodlines can grow thinner through intermarriage with leftover children.<br /> <br /> It looks to me as though a whole lot of information around the subject is written as though the assumption is not actually baseless, and the addition of that word is completely needless and adds contradiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T04:21:38-08:00","id":1279673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279590#post1279590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean them more to represent humans that can have Dragonblooded kids, like Kinfolk for the Garou. Like Dynasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a bad term for it, just one that's historically meant something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T04:40:17-08:00","id":1279674,"title":"","content":"It's what Holden called them in his Exalted vs World of Darkness thing that we're apparently not supposed to talk about cos the thread got deleted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T06:04:26-08:00","id":1279679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279674#post1279674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's what Holden called them in his Exalted vs World of Darkness thing that we're apparently not supposed to talk about cos the thread got deleted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. Not my doing but most of the places where I've seen it discussed Holden himself quickly became the primary subject matter rather than the work itself and in light of that I can appreciate a stance of &quot;no, not here.&quot; <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T06:16:29-08:00","id":1279683,"title":"","content":"Fair enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T08:04:18-08:00","id":1279702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279658#post1279658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks to me as though a whole lot of information around the subject is written as though the assumption is not actually baseless, and the addition of that word is completely needless and adds contradiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. IMO nothing about progenitive essence makes sense if it controls your children's chances of Exalting <i>without</i> impacting the strength of their bloodline. You'd basically be saying that Exaltation tends to skip a &quot;leftover&quot; child but doesn't change subsequent generations. In which case, as Eldagusto noticed above, we're back to Dragon's Nest breeding camps like before, but with crops of DB grandchildren rather than children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T08:22:56-08:00","id":1279706,"title":"","content":"I don't see how any of that is true. How well bred you are is a measure of how many mortal ancestors you have. It's got nothing to do with progenitive essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T08:52:28-08:00","id":1279715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279702#post1279702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. IMO nothing about progenitive essence makes sense if it controls your children's chances of Exalting <i>without</i> impacting the strength of their bloodline. You'd basically be saying that Exaltation tends to skip a &amp;quot;leftover&amp;quot; child but doesn't change subsequent generations. In which case, as Eldagusto noticed above, we're back to Dragon's Nest breeding camps like before, but with crops of DB grandchildren rather than children.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that still doesn't work. On a few counts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T09:46:49-08:00","id":1279726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279706#post1279706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how any of that is true. How well bred you are is a measure of how many mortal ancestors you have. It's got nothing to do with progenitive essence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's my takeaway as well. I think the sidebar at the start of Chapter 2 mentioning leftover children is a bit misleading because you can be a leftover child who does Exalt. Taking a pure eugenics take on bloodlines being inevitably diluted is problematic as well, but it's probably fair that the more mortal ancestry you have, the more likely you are to have a weak bloodline, but it's also a mystical/magical property. If it was capable of actually completely fading out, the Great Houses would likely already be in a lot of trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23811-taintedbalance","name":"TaintedBalance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23811_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T10:13:34-08:00","id":1279730,"title":"","content":"My current headcanon is that if there was ever any decline in the strength of the blood, then it plateaued about a thousand years before the Usurpation with little to no attempts at conserving it by the dragon blooded at the time. They just married whoever they felt like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T10:38:00-08:00","id":1279736,"title":"","content":"Progenitive Essence is currently in a state of being fine-tuned, so discussion about it is probably limited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T10:52:16-08:00","id":1279741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279706#post1279706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how any of that is true. How well bred you are is a measure of how many mortal ancestors you have. It's got nothing to do with progenitive essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the strength of your bloodline, which is a function of how strong your parents bloodlines were and so on, and which also determines how likely you and your descendants are to Exalt, right? And progenitive essence says that when it is high conceived children are more likely to Exalt and when it is low they are less likely, right? And you <i>personally</i> don't have to Exalt to carry a strong bloodline, right? (BTW these are not rhetorical questions; I expect maybe we disagree on one or more? But they're my postulates.)<br /> <br /> So if the two are independent, then when two high-Breeding people have a child when at a low-ebb of progenitive essence, that child is <i>less </i>likely to Exalt, but any grandchildren down that line are still equally likely to Exalt, right? Which doesn't make sense to me.<br /> <br /> Whereas if Breeding is just the expression of progenitive essence &quot;locked in&quot; at conception, that low-ebb child's lower chance of Exalting gets passed down in the form of lower Breeding. So having children too fast diminishes the bloodline in the same way, and by the same mechanism, as having children outside the bloodline does. Which I like because it's consistent and not game-able. EDIT: Or at least, maximization would be a matter of finding precise numerical values for immeasurable quantities. I still call that &quot;safe&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279715#post1279715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that still doesn't work. On a few counts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't it though? Wouldn't a bunch of coordinated, well-bred people be able to produce a large, low-quality second generation, and an even larger, high-quality <i>third</i> generation, well in excess of &quot;normal&quot; productivity, if Breeding travels down the line independent of progenitive essence? (&quot;quality&quot; in this case meaning &quot;propensity to Exalt&quot;). Because functionally that's what I meant.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this is good or right or desirable; quite the opposite. <i>But</i> the counterargument was always that it's a fairly sensible plan for a totalitarian regime (or the secret puppet masters backing the totalitarian regime). And all it takes to undo it is to assume that the &quot;strength of your blood&quot; that your children inherit is consumed at conception and has to recharge. Which is what it seems to me progenitive essence is doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 01-09-2019, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T11:45:25-08:00","id":1279749,"title":"","content":"A difference in breeding does not produce the mean of the two breeding levels. Two thin blooded mortals can produce a DB whose children will all have higher chance of exalting than any of the parents'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 01-09-2019, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T12:08:51-08:00","id":1279754,"title":"","content":"My assumption is that a mortal child of a dynast at full progenitive potential is as likely to have a dragon blooded kid as the mortal child of an outcaste or a mortal who failed to exalt because their parent's essence was spent. The only thing that changes it is how far back your last dragon blooded ancestor was. &quot;Well bred&quot; for a mortal is about keeping that percentage of dragon blooded ancestors high and it doesn't matter how pure the bloodline of that ancestor was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T13:34:55-08:00","id":1279769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279749#post1279749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A difference in breeding does not produce the mean of the two breeding levels. Two thin blooded mortals can produce a DB whose children will all have higher chance of exalting than any of the parents'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point, though I wasn't presuming mean, just &quot;some function&quot;. Stochastic functions count <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Or, to be more specific, your breeding is some function of your parents' progenitive essence, which in turn are functions of their respective breeding and time since their previous babies, if any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T14:26:29-08:00","id":1279782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279754#post1279754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My assumption is that a mortal child of a dynast at full progenitive potential is as likely to have a dragon blooded kid as the mortal child of an outcaste or a mortal who failed to exalt because their parent's essence was spent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then what does it mean for Dragonblooded to have different levels of Breeding? Was the idea of Exaltation being more common in some Dynastic families than others retconned out of existence and I missed it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279754#post1279754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that changes it is how far back your last dragon blooded ancestor was. &quot;Well bred&quot; for a mortal is about keeping that percentage of dragon blooded ancestors high and it doesn't matter how pure the bloodline of that ancestor was.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not quite sure how you would calculate that %. Would a child with 4 dragon-blooded grandparents and two mortal parents have the same odds as one with two DB parents (because all of their lines of descent hit DBs?)? Or do they go down because of the mortals in the middle?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T16:31:16-08:00","id":1279805,"title":"","content":"Ok, so I was modelling it like this: Say you have a mortal kid of a dragon blooded. If they have a kid with a mortal of no specific bloodline and the kid doesn't exalt, then their chances of having a kid who does will be lower than their parent's. If, however, that mortal has a kid with another child of a dragon blooded and their kid doesn't exalt, then that kid will have just as much chance to have a dragon blooded child as they did. <br /> <br /> The dragon blooded themselves aren't affected by this. They can be thin blooded just fine, and <i>that</i> is the bulk of what determines how many scions a house produces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T21:05:58-08:00","id":1279860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279782#post1279782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then what does it mean for Dragonblooded to have different levels of Breeding? Was the idea of Exaltation being more common in some Dynastic families than others retconned out of existence and I missed it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite. It is still a <b>setting detail</b>, just <i>not</i> a game mechanic. <br /> <br /> Your characters can follow the expectation, or be a statistical outlier, without needing dice rolls to make that determination.<br /> <br /> See also: Pg 143, Ex3 Dragonblooded, Breeding and Exaltation bluebox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-10T07:38:30-08:00","id":1279897,"title":"","content":"It's worth mentioning that the main thing progenitive essence does is preserve the integrity of the setting. It's there to stop the lone sorcerer with a neomah, or the outcaste king with many wives from having more Dragon-Blooded children than an entire Great House.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-10T12:27:15-08:00","id":1279943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279897#post1279897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth mentioning that the main thing progenitive essence does is preserve the integrity of the setting. It's there to stop the lone sorcerer with a neomah, or the outcaste king with many wives from having more Dragon-Blooded children than an entire Great House.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually curious if changing the setting will stop ideas of people already ignoring the setting.<br /> <br /> Still at least it might stop those that argued it would work out of the mechanics, which was simplified and not how the setting worked; or it might mean those type of players finds a new way to game the mechanics (higher ratio of males in their breeding camps, perhaps?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-10T16:58:42-08:00","id":1279995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1279943#post1279943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm actually curious if changing the setting will stop ideas of people already ignoring the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they were ignoring the setting though. Most Dragon-Blooded breeding schemes I've seen over the years were a misguided attempt to give Lunars an acomplishment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> or it might mean those type of players finds a new way to game the mechanics (higher ratio of males in their breeding camps, perhaps?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Some people are just very commited to rape.I don't care about those people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T00:20:08-08:00","id":1280061,"title":"","content":"What is the Overall population of Lookshy I wonder? Just so I can compare the DB numbers to something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T05:11:30-08:00","id":1280079,"title":"","content":"If they have 3,000 DBs and DBs make up 1% of the population, that makes a population of 300,000.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T15:10:26-08:00","id":1280185,"title":"","content":"I have some thoughts.<br /> <br /> And because the forum still doesn't work properly on my laptop browser and I have to do this on my phone, they'll be kind of piecemeal. Bear with me.<br /> <br /> First off, I've changed my mind about leftover children. I can actually see a background in which fine knowledge of how that affects bloodline becomes distorted by fear and prejudice (helped along a bit by parties with agendas). I can also see how that never gets fixed if nobody is willing to risk their own bloodline for the sake of experiment.<br /> <br /> For the sake of players and storytellers, I can actually see benefits to removing the complication from the actual function of breeding, and the main thing I liked about it (genealogy intrigue) would remain intact.<br /> <br /> So I've no beef with that, and will endeavour to find erroneous references to assist the developers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T00:41:13-08:00","id":1280278,"title":"","content":"Before I say aught else, I want to reiterate a perspective on progenitive Essence:<br /> <br /> If the only thing it did, or even primary thing, was cut off theorycrafting and/or close off holes in the lore, I would value it less, because I think that addressing observations like that shouldn't be the priority of any fiction, and is often likely to produce weak results.<br /> <br /> I find the primary value of the concept is that it creates compelling drama of its own, by adding an additional social layer to the matter of how the Dragon Blooded pass on their power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T03:40:00-08:00","id":1280286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1280278#post1280278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the primary value of the concept is that it creates compelling drama of its own, by adding an additional social layer to the matter of how the Dragon Blooded pass on their power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, that is an argument I buy. While I personally don't find that particular drama to be compelling, that's just my personal preference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T03:52:39-08:00","id":1280287,"title":"","content":"Re; progenitive essence for maintenance of the setting, I don't have a hate on it or anything, but I'm not too convinced it's needed as opposed to simpler and less impactful fixes like &quot;Neomah (or other magic breeding methods) are not so good for Dragonblooded essence&quot; or &quot;If you're an outcaste who can get enough high breeding women around to do that, and keep all this show on the road despite the challenges of the setting, then &quot;mazel tov&quot;. So far this hasn't happened.&quot;, that allow more rapid population expansions under the right conditions (but acknowledges those conditions as hard to achieve).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T04:10:14-08:00","id":1280291,"title":"","content":"For neomah, at least, I prefer where they came down because of the way that doesn't leave the mixed message of &quot;the setting contains escapist elements such as sorcery to overcome various kinds of inability to conceive children&quot; and saying that Terrestrial Exalted end up excluded from that and have a more strictly enforced heteronormativity.<br /> <br /> I know there's an argument about the idea that the setting might lend itself to a certain unsentimental presentation, but I... don't care? It's not something I don't care about in all instances, but for something like this, and considering the last few years, I don't care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T04:41:04-08:00","id":1280293,"title":"","content":"There are probably middle ways where you can alter the Neomah function to reduce sorcery baby factory type stuff while supporting same sex couple reproduction fantasy stuff to a degree that it's not hugely more or less difficult than the status quo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T04:52:33-08:00","id":1280296,"title":"","content":"Now, I don't have the books close by. But as far as I know, a Neomah creates a child from bits it bites of from the parents. So a &quot;normal&quot; child of a neomah usually has a hundred parents or more.<br /> <br /> While being a Dragon-Blood means faster healing rates, providing 50% of the material would mean some very serious wounds. Also, I can't see it increasing the chance of an exaltation. It definitely isn't a shortcut for producing offsprings.<br /> <br /> So I don't see having them as a way for those not falling into the fertile heterosexual category to have kids in any way means a potential population explosion of exalts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T05:08:25-08:00","id":1280298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1280296#post1280296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I don't have the books close by. But as far as I know, a Neomah creates a child from bits it bites of from the parents. So a &quot;normal&quot; child of a neomah usually has a hundred parents or more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neomah weave children from samples of flesh or sexual fluids donated for the project. <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Biting is not required. A multitude of donors <i>may</i> be used, typically not many; as the more numerous and varied the donors used, the more likely the child will develop an aberant personality.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T05:30:35-08:00","id":1280300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1280293#post1280293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are probably middle ways where you can alter the Neomah function to reduce sorcery baby factory type stuff while supporting same sex couple reproduction fantasy stuff to a degree that it's not hugely more or less difficult than the status quo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and it's right there in progenitive Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T05:32:50-08:00","id":1280302,"title":"","content":"That's <b>a</b> way, sure, not necessarily the most minimal or only way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T05:41:28-08:00","id":1280305,"title":"","content":"I keep being torn on how to approach Dragon Blooded and mortals of no breeding*. My first impulse is that it should drop the odds significantly; if a regular couple has a 50% chance, I don't think the odds for only one parent with the bloodline should be half that. That can be squared with the idea that each parent is providing more than just a percentage, and that it's more like each providing half the chromosomes.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I find the odd reference to inviting Dragon Blooded to marry into something like mortal royalty for the sake of adding a strain of the bloodline in. Maybe that should be something mostly concerned with the Well-Bred, with their odds reduced from 80% to something around 20.<br /> <br /> * I've noted that the Well-Bred Merit removed the Dragon Blooded prerequisite, so now it can apply to anybody with the right parents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T05:45:52-08:00","id":1280306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1280302#post1280302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's <b>a</b> way, sure, not necessarily the most minimal or only way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm all for not overly complicating the subject, but I think there's a point at which being minimal just leaves a lot of nagging unanswered questions. I think that point is only a few steps below where we are now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T05:59:05-08:00","id":1280307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1280298#post1280298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neomah weave children from samples of flesh or sexual fluids donated for the project. <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Biting is not required. A multitude of donors <i>may</i> be used, typically not many; as the more numerous and varied the donors used, the more likely the child will develop an aberant personality.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, and the amount needed by only using sexual fluids means a load of encounters to have the material. Or are we talking hentai amount per load here?<br /> <br /> That is my point. You can do it with a neomah, without being hurt, but that take a load of time. Or it can be quick, but hurt like hell. Neither is a shortcut, or a solution to those wanting an army of DBs starting with just a few.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T07:06:53-08:00","id":1280318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1280307#post1280307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, and the amount needed by only using sexual fluids means a load of encounters to have the material. Or are we talking hentai amount per load here?<br /> <br /> That is my point. You can do it with a neomah, without being hurt, but that take a load of time. Or it can be quick, but hurt like hell. Neither is a shortcut, or a solution to those wanting an army of DBs starting with just a few.</div> </div> </div> </div>It only takes one day, and there is no indication of ill effect on the donors. Where are you getting... Wait...<br /> <br /> ( Okay, checking 2ed core, and 1ed GoD... Oh, I see... )<br /> <br /> Ah. No. It seems that has been amended. Ex3 does not suggest that the neomah requires an entire baby mass of donations for the project, nor that it is a long and arduous project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T09:32:27-08:00","id":1280332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1280318#post1280318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It only takes one day, and there is no indication of ill effect on the donors. Where are you getting... Wait...<br /> <br /> ( Okay, checking 2ed core, and 1ed GoD... Oh, I see... )<br /> <br /> Ah. No. It seems that has been amended. Ex3 does not suggest that the neomah requires an entire baby mass of donations for the project, nor that it is a long and arduous project.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I agree that is a reason for progenetive essense. As long no one blame earlier editions on that rewrite of neomah, I won't argue against it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T08:35:58-08:00","id":1280483,"title":"","content":"Problem is the old limitation on Neomah was more of an issue to the infertile/same sex couple than the sorcerer who wants to build an army.<br /> <br /> It doesn't have to be 50:50, it you're willing to sacrifice a captive or a slave as the second donor then the average adult male (83.9 kg) has enough mass to make almost 24 newborn children (3.5 kg).<br /> <br /> If the fianc\u00e9e and I wanted a demon baby then 1.75 kg of genetic material is a huge undertaking and I guess we could save up years worth of hair, blood and toenail clippings ...but if that's kosher, can't the sorcerer just carve up a well-preserved corpse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 01-13-2019, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T08:56:05-08:00","id":1280488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1280483#post1280483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem is the old limitation on Neomah was more of an issue to the infertile/same sex couple than the sorcerer who wants to build an army.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, splitting 3,5kg (I think the average was closer to 3kg just a few decades ago) with 266 day would mean 13,16g per day, which then could be split over both parents. Then there is also the option to let it take longer time.<br /> <br /> So, problem and issue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T16:37:04-08:00","id":1280570,"title":"","content":"Neomah flesh crafting is one of those things that I judge as having always been way overthought. On several counts. Relevant here is that, offhand, I can recall no reference to the idea that crafting a baby requires a quantity of tissue equal to the mass of the baby. I see no narrative value to such a constraint, because neomah look like a basic utility demon, weird in the manner of their kind.<br /> <br /> Maybe there's the reference to how they only craft for their own business when they have &quot;enough&quot; material, but I've generally read that as demonic arbitrariness rather than a necessary constraint.<br /> <br /> (Making armies with neomah is a bit silly, or at least requires about the same commitment as building an army any other way; you start off with lots of babies, and how many years is it going to be before they can fight? Where is their food coming from?<br /> <br /> Really, that's often gone for lots of ideas about the Dragon Blooded as well.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T17:32:11-08:00","id":1280578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1280570#post1280570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Making armies with neomah is a bit silly, or at least requires about the same commitment as building an army any other way; you start off with lots of babies, and how many years is it going to be before they can fight? Where is their food coming from?<br /> <br /> Really, that's often gone for lots of ideas about the Dragon Blooded as well.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars are frequently the elephant in the room in these discussions, because this is exactly how they've been operating for the last two editions. Places like Dzibilchan came to occupy the quasi-canon state they do because &quot;breed my own Dragon-Blooded&quot; has only been ignored as an option for them due to deeply rooted prejudice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":1115,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","user":"The Hug Ninja","date":". 01-13-2019, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T04:25:40-08:00","id":1280667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277743-so-lookshy-has-what-like-a-hundred-times-the-concentration-of-exalted?p=1280578#post1280578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars are frequently the elephant in the room</div> </div> </div> </div> I see what you did, there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 01-14-2019, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T05:57:30-08:00","id":1280677,"title":"","content":"Lets say the Isolationist Faction gains prominence, what would Lookshy work on in a ten year plan? Would they expand outposts into towns? Would they use arcane technics to expand the housing for the city like maybe up or down of spatially folded?<br /> <br /> How much of Lookshys population is outside of their Citystate? If a truly huge amount then does Lookshy have a tradition of just flat out not owning a much more then you can travel with, or perhaps having family homes where they can send their possessions?<br /> <br /> What is the point of making Lookshy Patriarchal besides the trope of them being a mirror of the Realm. It reminds of other fictional rivals like Tevinter\u2019s Chantry being Patriarchal and The Orthodox Chantry being matriarchal in Dragon Age. I mean Lookshy is even more egalitarian with the sexes then the Realm that seems enough to me. But why are they Patriarchal, besides the useful trope of just being the weird upside down rivals? Was the Shogunate Patriarchal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}